28:    Rule
29:    - For every 8-connected yellow object, find the unique plus center whose
30:      in-bounds center/up/down/left/right cells contain the yellow object and no
31:      black cells.
32:    - Recolor the grey cells of that plus red; keep yellow and black cells fixed.
33:
34:    Key insight
35:    - The yellow pixels are partial cross markers, and the surrounding grey cells
36:      in the same cross are the missing cells to highlight.
37:    """
38:    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
39:    assert g.ndim == 2, "expected a 2D grid"
40:    height, width = map(int, g.shape)
41:    assert height > 0 and width > 0, "expected a nonempty grid"
42:
43:    empty = Color.BLACK
44:    marker = Color.YELLOW
45:    grey = Color.GREY
46:    red = Color.RED
47:    assert set(map(int, np.unique(g))) <= {empty, marker, grey}, "expected only black, yellow, and grey input colors"
48:
49:    out = g.copy()
50:    yellow_objects = components_mask(g == marker, connectivity=8)
51:    assert yellow_objects, "expected at least one yellow marker object"
52:
53:    for coords in yellow_objects:
